  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the reaction,<br ><math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>Q</mtext> <mo>→</mo> <mtext>R</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>S</mtext> </mrow> </math><br >the time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></math> reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo> </mo></math>is twice the time taken for<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>. The concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo> </mo></math>varies with reaction time as shown in the figure.The overall order of the reaction is:<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0020_b859d309593b.png\"/>  </p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
